<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Bolts</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1739–1808</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Bolts was a Dutch-born merchant and former servant of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> after quarrels with its government. He persuaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> to back a trading venture to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and Asia, and in 1777 founded the short-lived Austrian settlement on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delagoa-bay">Delagoa Bay</a>.</p></div>
